A change to libkrun 1.19.7. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, like libkrun.

The VM gives its free memory back to macOS. A backport of libkrun PR #931
(https://github.com/libkrun/libkrun/pull/931), which is in libkrun 2.0 but not in 1.19.x:
when the guest reports free pages, the VMM worker unmaps them from the guest, replaces them
with new anonymous memory (mmap MAP_FIXED), and maps them again. madvise() frees nothing
for memory that is mapped into a VM of Hypervisor.framework.

Upstream commits in this patch:
- 4144d3dcb6 vmm: end the worker thread when its channel is closed
- 9141d35b74 vmm/macos: add a worker message that reclaims guest RAM
- 04736a19c8 virtio/balloon: give reported free pages back to the host on macOS
- 1ef5f9a84d vmm: break the worker ownership cycle
- 137f84bdf7 utils/eventfd: honor EFD_NONBLOCK as a bitflag on macOS

Changes for 1.19.x:
- The 2.0 API (BalloonDevice::set_free_page_reporting_mode) is not in 1.x. libkrun attaches
  the balloon itself, so src/vmm/src/builder.rs sets FreePageReportingMode::Replace on macOS.
- src/libkrun/src/lib.rs starts the VMM worker on macOS also without the GPU (as upstream
  f3c3c000ef does for 2.0).
- The unit tests in balloon/macos.rs use the InterruptTransport of 1.19.x.

